## Version Control Rule

- **{{author}} commits manually.** Never run `git commit`, `git push`, `git reset --hard`, or history-rewriting commands unless **{{author}}** explicitly instructs you to in the current turn.
- Leave working trees clean of temporary files, unredacted `.env` secrets, or local database dumps.

## Mandatory Verification Gates

Before reporting any task complete:

1. Run the project's formatter, linter/static checks, type checker, and test suite.
2. Verify all boundary/invariant tests still pass (`domain/` stays free of I/O, clock, and network side effects).
3. Update `AGENTS/STATE.md` (and `AGENTS/HANDOFF.md` if architecture shifts) with what changed, what commands actually ran, and any remaining open items.
4. Write an immutable working log in gitignored `AGENTS/AGENTS_LOGS/LOG_YYYYMMDD_HHMMSS_<AGENT>.md` (never overwrite an older log).
5. Never fabricate or extrapolate passing checks—report exact command results only.
